title: Real-time strategy
intro: Units, workers, buildings, fog of war and a computer opponent, all as components, and a Strategy template that's a whole game to play.
project: Strategy | Ironvale

chapter: A strategy game from components | The Strategy template
say: The new Strategy template is a complete real-time strategy game, made only of components, with no code.
select: Main Camera
explain: component:Commander | Commander | The Commander on the camera is the player's controls. Click or drag to select, right-click to send units, a command card with hotkeys, and a minimap.
explain: component:FogOfWar | Fog of War | Fog of War hides whatever your units can't see.
select: Enemy Team
explain: component:Faction | Faction | Each side is a Faction, with its color and the gold and wood it has to spend.
explain: component:Opponent | Opponent | An Opponent lets the computer play a side. It gathers, builds, trains an army, and attacks.
set: Opponent.TrainEvery = 25
explain: field:Opponent.TrainEvery | Train Every | Train Every sets how hard it plays. For this demo, an easy game: a new soldier every twenty five seconds.
browse: Worker
explain: catalog:docs | Strategy components | Units, workers, buildings, producers, resources and fighters are components too, ready for your own games.
click: catalog:close

chapter: Gather and build | Select, right-click, hotkeys
play
wait: 1.5
say: Our base is in the bottom left. Red is out there somewhere, in the dark.
gamedrag: -19.4, -4.2, -14.2, -5.8
say: Drag a box round the five workers to select them,
gameorder: -21, -3.5
say: then right-click the gold mine. They carry gold back to the town hall, load after load.
explain: hud:resources | Resources | Gold goes up with every load. Supply says how many units we can field.
explain: hud:card | Command card | The command card shows what the selection can do, each with its hotkey.
tap: B
gameclick: -13, -2
say: B, and a click, puts up a barracks. The nearest worker goes off to build it.
tap: F
gameclick: -11, -9
say: F adds a farm, for more supply.
gameclick: -16, -8
tap: W
tap: W
say: Click the town hall and press W twice to train two more workers.
wait: 2

chapter: Train an army | Barracks, control groups, rally point, minimap
ready: Barracks | 40
gameclick: -13, -2
tap: S
tap: S
tap: S
tap: S
tap: S
say: The barracks is up. Select it, and press S to train soldiers, as many as we can pay for.
tap: LeftControl+D2
say: Control 2 keeps it as group two, to pick it again from anywhere.
gameorder: -9, -4
say: A right-click sets the rally point, where new soldiers gather.
explain: hud:selection | Training | They train one after another, paid for up front.
say: While they train, click the minimap to look around. Red's base is up in the top right, hidden by the fog.
minimap: 6, 4
wait: 2
minimap: -10, -6
afford: 180 Gold | 60
tap: D2
tap: S
tap: S
tap: S
say: Press 2 for the barracks, and S for more soldiers as the gold comes in.
afford: 180 Gold | 60
tap: D2
tap: S
tap: S
tap: S
afford: 180 Gold | 60
tap: D2
tap: S
tap: S
tap: S
say: An army needs time. Let's wait for a dozen soldiers.
have: 12 Soldier | 150

chapter: Attack | Attack-move, reinforcements, victory
gamedrag: -14, -1.5, -4, -8
say: Drag round the army,
tap: LeftControl+D1
say: and Control 1 keeps them as group one.
tap: A
minimap: 15, 8
say: A, then a click on the minimap, sends them across the map to fight their way into red's base.
tap: D2
minimaporder: 13, 6
say: Back at the barracks, a right-click on the minimap sends new soldiers straight to the front.
afford: 120 Gold | 30
tap: S
tap: S
tap: D1
tap: D1
say: Pressing 1 twice brings the camera to the army.
wait: 8
tap: D1
tap: D1
say: Red fights back, and its tower fires arrows. Anything that's hurt shows its health.
wait: 10
tap: D1
tap: D1
wait: 10
tap: D1
tap: D1
say: Red rebuilds what it loses, so we keep pushing until its last building falls.
waitfor: Victory | 240
say: Victory. The Commander opens the Victory panel by itself, and Play Again starts over.
wait: 2
stop
